    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i'm having some trouble with some walnut joinery. i'm cutting dovetails but the tips of the pins keep splintering or tearing out slightly. what am I doing wrong?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like the dovetail saw might not be properly set or the material is too thick for the blade's teeth. Ensure that your saw is sharp and exactly parallel to the joinery line, and adjust your technique accordingly so that the blade cuts cleanly along the silhouette. Also, use a high-quality dovetail pin gauge to consistently size the pins for accuracy. Adjust to avoid sliding the blade and damaging the material.",
